1679 PAIR PICTURE
  T = <+ t1 | - t2 >     gcd(t1,t2)=1

       t1 yes          t2 not
         \               /
          coprime pair

  All S are P is two nestings at once:
       s contains p     and     sigma contains pi

ONE VISUAL STEP
  Claim:  man contains animal
  Picture:   man [ animal ]
  Numbers:   6 = 2*3 ,  2|6
  Geometry:  animal-mark is a proper part of man-mark
  The three inscriptions stand or fall together.
  That is a characteristic: the diagram is already the argument.

WHAT THE PICTURES HANDLE
  combination, containment, overlap, exclusion

WHAT THEY DO NOT HANDLE BY THEMSELVES
  higher-order properties, continuity,
  the true primitives of nature

RULE
  A diagram here is a readable combination, not a map of the world.
